{
  "_comment": [
    "Entity pool for the semantic generator. Each row is one reading of one",
    "surface form; a form with several readings is listed several times,",
    "which is how an ambiguous name is represented.",
    "",
    "Fields: text (surface form, exactly as it must appear in a sentence),",
    "labels (ontology labels), type (ontology type name, optional),",
    "named (true for proper names), preposition (what the form takes as an",
    "adjunct: 'at noon' but 'on Monday'), appositive (a gloss that settles",
    "the reading in context), property_head / property_degree (the",
    "adjective already inside the form, kept decomposed).",
    "",
    "Held-out splits are derived from the surface form by a stable hash, so",
    "adding a row never moves an existing one between splits.",
    "Entries after the curated ones were mined from data/eng-base.jsonl with semantic_generator.mining and reviewed by hand; see STATUS_RU.md."
  ],
